Wazuh SIEM Integration — AD Home Lab Extension

Extends the AD-Home-Lab environment with a SIEM stack and a dedicated attacker VM, moving the lab from "AD infrastructure" into SOC/blue-team territory: log ingestion, detection engineering, and (next milestone) incident write-ups against a simulated attack.

Why

Deploying and enrolling infrastructure is only half of a SOC-relevant skill set — the other half is seeing what that infrastructure reports and knowing how to interpret it. This phase adds a Wazuh manager to collect and correlate logs from DC1, and a Kali Linux VM to generate real attack traffic against it, so the detection pipeline can be tested end-to-end rather than just configured.

