Two new VMs join the existing DC1/Client1 pair, following the same dual-homing pattern already established in the base lab: intnet for internal traffic, NAT only where internet access is genuinely needed (package installs).

Build: Wazuh-Manager

Spec: Ubuntu Server 26.04, 4096 MB RAM, 2 vCPU, dual-homed (NAT + intnet), static IP 172.16.0.10 on the internal adapter.

Static IP was set via netplan rather than DHCP, keeping it consistent with how DC1 and Client1 are addressed in the base lab:

yaml
network:
  version: 2
  ethernets:
    enp0s3:
      dhcp4: true
    enp0s8:
      dhcp4: false
      addresses: [172.16.0.10/24]

Wazuh itself installs via the official all-in-one script:

bash
curl -O https://packages.wazuh.com/4.9/wazuh-install.sh
sudo bash wazuh-install.sh -a
Issues hit and resolved
Issue	Cause	Fix
vmwgfx DRM error on boot	Newer Ubuntu kernel's graphics driver incompatible with VirtualBox's default VMSVGA emulation	Changed Graphics Controller to VBoxSVGA in VM Display settings
Static IP not applying after netplan apply	File permissions warning + systemd-networkd not running cleanly on first reload	chmod 600 on the netplan config, then explicit systemctl restart systemd-networkd before re-applying
curl hanging / silently failing	Typo (-s0 instead of -sO) plus curl not yet installed	Installed curl via apt, corrected the flag
Installer failed hardware check	VM under-provisioned relative to Wazuh's stated minimum (4GB RAM / 2 CPU) for the OpenSearch-based indexer	Powered off, bumped Base Memory to 4096 MB and CPU count to 2 in VirtualBox settings before retrying
