Build: Kali-Attacker

Spec: Kali Linux (pre-built VirtualBox image), 2048 MB RAM, 2 vCPU, intnet only — no NAT adapter, matching the same isolation intent already applied to Client1. This VM should only ever see the lab network, not the open internet.

Rather than going through VirtualBox's Import Appliance wizard (which expects .ovf/.ova and doesn't recognize the extracted .vbox/.vdi pair Kali ships), the VM was built manually:

New VM → Linux / Debian (64-bit) — no dedicated "Kali" OS type exists, Kali is Debian-based
Skipped ISO/unattended install
Use an Existing Virtual Hard Disk File → registered the extracted .vdi via Virtual Media Manager → Add
Adapter 1 set to Internal Network intnet, static IP 172.16.0.66/24 configured manually through NetworkManager
